    declaration: struct-decl #29 1414:32:1-2332:43:1 name="@3::Hooks" doc="The hooks of a feature, for `run`. They run in the worker that runs the scenarios (`agentica test` keeps one\nworker per `--jobs` lane), so once for each feature and each worker, not once for each run: with `--jobs 4` a\nfeature may start up to four times."
      field: field-decl #22 1890:37:3-1934:38:1 name="before_all" doc="Runs before the first scenario of the feature that the worker takes, in a task that stays until `after_all`, so\nthe handles it opens (a server program, a listener) belong to it and outlive the scenarios. What it returns is\nwhat `feature_state` gives every scenario of the feature on that worker. An error, a crash or a time out is\n`RUNTIME-BDD-BEFORE-ALL`: that scenario fails, and the others of the feature on that worker are not executed."
        type: type-ref #21 1902:37:15-1933:37:46 name="Fn"
          arg: type-ref #18 1905:37:18-1912:37:25 name="@3::Feature"
          arg: type-ref #20 1914:37:27-1932:37:45 name="Result"
            arg: type-ref #19 1921:37:34-1931:37:44 name="JSON.Value"
      field: field-decl #28 2279:41:3-2328:42:1 name="after_all" doc="Runs when the worker leaves the feature (the next scenario is of another feature, or the lane has no more),\nwith what `before_all` returned, in the task that ran `before_all`. A worker that a failed scenario ended runs\nnone: its handles close with it. An error or a crash is `RUNTIME-BDD-AFTER-ALL`, at the file of the feature."
        type: type-ref #27 2290:41:14-2327:41:51 name="Fn"
          arg: type-ref #23 2293:41:17-2300:41:24 name="@3::Feature"
          arg: type-ref #24 2302:41:26-2312:41:36 name="JSON.Value"
          arg: type-ref #26 2314:41:38-2326:41:50 name="Result"
            arg: type-ref #25 2321:41:45-2325:41:49 name="Void"
